virglrenderer: Venus submits only ended primaries whose secondaries are what they executed

What: a command buffer gets a serial, one more at each begin, reset and pool reset (also
of a pool's freed secondaries a primary still holds), whatever the driver's call returns,
and an executable flag (set by a successful end, cleared by a begin, reset, pool reset or
free). vkCmdExecuteCommands keeps the serial of each secondary in the primary's held entry
(virgl-venus-secondary-holds.patch). vkQueueSubmit and vkQueueSubmit2 refuse, before any
driver call, a command buffer that is not an ended primary, and a primary whose secondary
was begun, reset or had its pool reset since the primary executed it; the primary's
vkEndCommandBuffer refuses the latter too. A refusal ends the app's context. Vulkan calls
all of these invalid, so a legal app never meets them.
Why: both drivers read a secondary's commands after vkCmdExecuteCommands. MoltenVK encodes
the secondary's current content when it encodes the primary (at vkQueueSubmit, at the
primary's vkEndCommandBuffer with MVK_CONFIG_PREFILL_METAL_COMMAND_BUFFERS);
KosmicKrisp replays it at a reusable primary's 2nd and later submit (kk_queue.c,
vk_command_buffer.c). vkr checked the Metal passes a secondary opens and the pass it
continues at the execute (virgl-venus-encoder-cap.patch, virgl-venus-command-state.patch),
so a secondary recorded again with more passes got past the cap below which Metal keeps
QEMU alive. Nothing checked what was submitted: MoltenVK refuses a secondary and a 2nd
submit of a one-time buffer itself (MVKCommandBuffer::canExecute), KosmicKrisp relies on
the app. Both drivers read secondaries inside vkQueueSubmit on the calling thread (MoltenVK's
MVK_CONFIG_SYNCHRONOUS_QUEUE_SUBMITS is 1, KosmicKrisp submits in Mesa's immediate mode),
which the holds rely on (#676).
Upstream: OmacVM policy (VUID-vkQueueSubmit-pCommandBuffers-00070, -00071, -00072,
VUID-vkEndCommandBuffer-commandBuffer-00059).
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-commands.c (c-state-secondary-held-resubmit-ok, -rerecord-ok,
-rerecord-submit, -reset-submit, -pool-reset-submit, -free-pool-reset-submit,
-rerecord-end, s-submit-secondary, -recording, -initial, h-release-secondary-ok; also under
libgmalloc).

